# GRADSKOOL — Railway Procfile
#
# web workers/threads (2026-08-15): dropped from --workers 2 --threads 4 to
# --workers 1 --threads 3 — the Hobby-tier service is hard-capped at 1GB RAM
# (Railway Settings → Scale → Replica Limits), and 2 full worker processes
# each carrying their own copy of Django/DRF/Celery/Pillow/Sentry in memory
# was enough baseline alone to tip into OOM SIGKILLs the moment a PDF page
# watermark request landed on top. One worker halves that baseline; 3 threads
# still allows a few concurrent requests without adding a second full worker's
# import overhead. If this ever feels too serialized under real traffic, the
# actual fix is upgrading off Hobby's 1GB cap, not raising workers back up.
#
# Three processes to deploy on Railway:
#   web    → Django (gunicorn) — handles API requests
#   worker → Celery worker     — runs async tasks (drip emails, transcription, AI notes)
#   beat   → Celery Beat       — schedules periodic tasks (drip send loop every 15 min)
#
# Deploy on Railway:
#   1. Create one service per process
#   2. Set the start command for each service
#   3. All three share the same repo + env vars

web:    python manage.py collectstatic --noinput && gunicorn config.wsgi:application --bind 0.0.0.0:$PORT --workers 1 --threads 3 --timeout 120
worker: celery -A config.celery worker --loglevel=info -Q default,high_priority --concurrency 2
beat:   celery -A config.celery beat --loglevel=info
